+#### `hide-from-own-capture`
+
+<sup>Since: next release</sup>
+
+Set to `true` to leave the surface and its popups out of screen captures made by the client that owns it.
+Captures made by everyone else still show it as usual.
+
+This is for overlays that draw something based on a live capture of the screen underneath them, like a magnifier or a screen effect.
+Without this rule, such an overlay would see itself in its own capture.
+
+It applies to the wlr-screencopy and ext-image-copy-capture protocols.
+
+```kdl
+// Let a magnifier capture the screen under it without seeing itself.
+layer-rule {
+    match namespace="^magnifier$"
+
+    hide-from-own-capture true
+}
+```
+
 #### `opacity`
 
 Set the opacity of the surface.
